  "samIpa#g0"
 ],
 "known_non_equivalences": [
  "the call SHAPE is production's here — one presplit group per call, via headless_worker.build_fragment_prompt — but the rig still does not run through the coordinator/profile lane, so it carries no profile slot, no heal/bisect ladder and no kill gate. A group that would be healed or bisected in production is simply recorded as failed here. Both arms are affected identically, so the paired A-vs-B comparison is unharmed; absolute figures are not production figures.",
  "PREP context is per-CARD, and a fragment call carries only part of that card, so arm B gives a group the whole card's context. That is the design under test, not a defect — but it means arm B's context block does not shrink with the group, and a cost comparison must read it that way.",
  "manifest schema is pwg.headless_execution_manifest.v1 (unbound): a measurement rig, never a bulk execution path.",
  "the manifest declares model claude-sonnet-5 as the LANE default; both arms explicitly request claude-opus-5 and the returned model is attested per call."
 ],
